verdict: FALSIFICATION TRIGGERED (barrier rel 0.227 >> 1e-6). Our GL quadrature (n=32/64) does NOT
  reach the barrier. The integrand cos(z*u) oscillates with period ~2*pi/6e10 ~ 1e-10 in u; GL
  n=32/64 on [0,2] (node spacing ~0.03) aliases it. To reproduce t_0=2.217e4 with our tools we
  need the AFE (Approximate Functional Equation) or to run the Polymath15 C code directly.
note: degree-diff is a heuristic error estimate (|Q2-Q1|), not a rigorous bound; but 0.227 rel is
  ~27 orders of magnitude above the 1e-29 we need, so the "does not converge" conclusion is robust.
  The exact X0 value (6e10+83951.5) is from the local model's docstring; the conclusion is robust
  to the exact X0 (any X0 ~ 1e10 gives rapid oscillation).
